  "title": "The Render Queue Picnic",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "creative-work struggles",
  "premise": "A creator wants to use a waiting period well but keeps refreshing an animated render meter, causing their imaginary chair to grow roots. They place a visible notification bell beside the screen, prepare a tiny picnic on the desk, and return when the completed frame appears as the picnic’s final placemat.",
  "hook": "Refresh. Refresh. Still a sandwich-sized wait.",
  "visible_action": "Refresh icon spins; chair sprouts cartoon roots; bell is set; food-shaped paper props unfold; bell rings and completed image slides out.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "A waiting process can have a clear return signal.",
  "gate": "The render result is part of the fiction; do not imply any real render has been run or predict real processing time.",
